cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use BerryBrain, cite this software release and the accompanying article."
title: "BerryBrain: Keeping Derived Knowledge Consistent with Its Sources in Personal Knowledge Management"
type: software
version: "1.5.1"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24058185"
date-released: 2026-11-16
abstract: >-
  BerryBrain is a self-hosted personal knowledge management system and RAG architecture that keeps
  user-authored Markdown canonical, treats semantic graphs, retrieval indexes, and synthesized
  insights as provenance-linked rebuildable state governed by an operational ontology, an admission
  gate, and a two-note minimum-support invariant (MIN_INSIGHT_SUPPORT_NOTES = 2), and records human
  feedback as scoped, reversible policies.
